      "explanation": "<p><b>(A) Valium – (4) Tranquilizer</b> <br/><br/>A tranquilizer drug became a standard drug for the treatment of anxiety and one of most commonly prescribed drugs of all time.</p>\n\n<p><b>(B) Morphine – (3) Analgesic</b> <br/><br/>Morphine is effective for both acute and chronic pain and often used before and after surgery.</p>\n\n<p><b>(C) Norethindrone – (1) Antifertility drug</b> <br/><br/>It is a form of progesterone, a female hormone important for regulating ovulation and menstruation.</p>\n\n<p><b>(D) Vitamin B<sub>12</sub> – (2) Pernicious anaemia</b> <br/><br/>It is a nutrient that helps to keep our body blood cells and nerve cells healthy and help in making DNA.</p>"
